<% page_title "Music you are cleared to publish" %>
<% page_description "Subscribe to a genre, download full-length 48 kHz masters, and keep a dated licence record for every file. AI Pop Music licenses AI-generated songs for commercial work." %>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] lg:items-start">
    <div>
      <p class="meta uppercase">Licensed catalogue</p>

      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">
        Publish music you are cleared to use, without the licensing guesswork.
      </h1>

      <p class="measure mt-6 text-lg text-ink-600">
        Subscribe to the genres you work in. Download full-length 48 kHz masters, not loops
        or 30-second clips. Every download records the licence version it was granted under,
        so when a platform asks where your soundtrack came from, you have the answer.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <%= link_to "Choose your genres", plans_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
        <%= link_to "Hear the catalogue", genres_path, class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
      </div>

      <p class="meta mt-4">
        From $5 a month. Cancel any time; downloads you already made stay licensed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%# Concrete facts, in place of the testimonials a new catalogue does not have. %>
    <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-8 border-t border-paper-100 pt-8 lg:border-t-0 lg:pt-0">
      <div>
        <dt class="meta uppercase">Masters</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-600">48 kHz stereo FLAC, full length</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="meta uppercase">Downloads</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-600">Unlimited inside your genres</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="meta uppercase">Licence</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-600">Commercial use, version recorded per download</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="meta uppercase">Provenance</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-600">Generated on our own hardware, model and seed kept</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap mt-20">
  <div class="measure">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">The part that usually goes wrong</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-600">
      "Royalty-free" usually means a licence you cannot check, a track someone else may also
      have licensed to a hundred other channels, and no paperwork if a claim lands months
      later. You end up choosing between music you cannot prove you are allowed to use and
      music everyone has already heard.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="measure mt-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">What you get instead</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-ink-600">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink-950">A licence you can produce.</strong>
        Every download writes a record against your account: which track, which terms, which
        day. It is the difference between "I think I am allowed to use this" and a dated entry
        you can send to a platform.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink-950">Songs, not snippets.</strong>
        Full-length stereo masters you can score a whole piece with, edit, loop and mix into
        your work, rather than a bed that fades out mid-sentence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink-950">Music that fits the edit.</strong>
        Genres are organised by what you are making, and every track page lists tempo, key,
        duration and mood, so you can match the cut instead of auditioning blindly.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap mt-20">
  <h2 class="text-2xl">How it works</h2>
  <ol class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <li class="card p-5">
      <p class="meta uppercase">01</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-display text-lg">Pick a plan and your genres</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
        A plan covers a number of genres. Change which ones whenever you like; the price stays
        the same.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card p-5">
      <p class="meta uppercase">02</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-display text-lg">Download what you need</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
        Preview anything without an account. Subscribe and the masters unlock, with the licence
        recorded as you take them.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card p-5">
      <p class="meta uppercase">03</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-display text-lg">Publish and keep the record</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
        Use the tracks in videos, podcasts, streams, games and client work. Your download
        history stays as the proof.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="wrap mt-20">
  <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Start with a genre</h2>
    <%= link_to "All genres", genres_path, class: "text-sm underline" %>
  </div>

  <% if @genres.any? %>
    <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <% @genres.each do |genre| %>
        <li>
          <%= link_to genre_path(genre), class: "card block p-5 hover:border-ink-600" do %>
            <p class="font-display text-xl"><%= genre.name %></p>
            <p class="meta mt-2"><%= pluralize(genre.track_count, "track") %></p>
            <% if genre.description.present? %>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-600 line-clamp-2"><%= genre.description %></p>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  <% else %>
    <p class="mt-6 text-ink-600">
      The catalogue is being prepared. <%= link_to "See the plans", plans_path, class: "underline" %>
      to be ready when tracks land.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</section>

<% if @recent_tracks.any? %>
  <section class="wrap mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Recently added</h2>
    <ul class="mt-6 divide-y divide-paper-100 border-y border-paper-100">
      <% @recent_tracks.each do |track| %>
        <%= render "tracks/track_row", track: track, entitled: false %>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </section>
<% end %>

<% faqs = {
  "Can I really use these tracks commercially?" =>
    "Yes. An active subscription licenses every track in the genres your plan covers for commercial use, " \
    "including monetised videos, podcasts, client work and games. The licence page lists exactly what is " \
    "granted and what is not.",
  "What happens if a platform flags my video?" =>
    "Send us the order or download record and we will confirm the licence. Your account keeps a dated entry " \
    "for every file you have taken, which is the point of recording it at download time.",
  "What if I cancel?" =>
    "Downloads stop straight away and your genres stop being available. Work you already published stays " \
    "licensed under the terms in force when you downloaded it, so a released project is not put at risk.",
  "Is this music unique to me?" =>
    "Every track is generated from a recorded prompt and seed, and that provenance is stored with the track. " \
    "We do not resell the same master as a stock library item, and you are not competing with a hundred other " \
    "channels using the identical file.",
  "Do I need to credit you?" =>
    "No. Attribution is welcome and is never a condition of the licence."
} %>

<section class="wrap mt-20">
  <h2 class="text-2xl">Questions that decide it</h2>
  <dl class="measure mt-6 divide-y divide-paper-100 border-y border-paper-100">
    <% faqs.each do |question, answer| %>
      <div class="py-5">
        <dt class="font-display text-lg"><%= question %></dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600"><%= answer %></dd>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>
</section>

<%= structured_data(faq_structured_data(faqs)) %>

<section class="wrap mt-20">
  <div class="card flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-6 p-8">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl">Find your genre, start today</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-600">
        From $5 a month. Preview everything first - no account needed to listen.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Choose your genres", plans_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
      <%= link_to "Browse by genre", genres_path, class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
